 II of León", "context": "Alfonso IV succeeded his uncle Fruela II as King of León in 925, following a period of succession disputes."}, {"sourceSlug": "alfonso-iv-of-león", "sourceName": "Alfonso IV of León", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "ramiro-ii-of-leon", "targetName": "Ramiro II of León", "context": "Alfonso IV's abdication in 931 directly led to his brother Ramiro II ascending to the throne of León."}, {"sourceSlug": "ramiro-ii-of-leon", "sourceName": "Ramiro II of León", "verb": "TRANSFORMS", "targetSlug": "alfonso-iv-of-león", "targetName": "Alfonso IV of León", "context": "Ramiro II's capture and blinding of Alfonso IV in 932 fundamentally transformed Alfonso's status from monarch to imprisoned monk."}]}, {"timestamp": "2026-06-17T23:54:52Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#27726697159", "field": "detailsJson.places", "oldValue": [{"name": "Kingdom of Leon", "role": "Birth place"}], "newValue": [{"name": "León, Spain", "role": "Capital and seat of power"}, {"name": "Sahagún, Spain", "role": "Monastery of initial retirement"}, {"name": "Astorga, Spain", "role": "Site of imprisonment and blinding"}]}, {"timestamp": "2026-06-17T23:54:52Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#27726697159", "field": "subjects", "oldValue": ["Monarchs & Rulers"], "newValue": ["Kingdom of León", "Monarchy", "Medieval Spain", "Reconquista", "Abdication", "Dynastic Conflict", "Monasticism", "Early Middle Ages", "Iberian Peninsula", "Christianity"]}, {"timestamp": "2026-06-17T23:54:52Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#27726697159", "field": "frameworks", "oldValue": ["POLITICAL_SYSTEMS", "EMPIRE_AND_COLONIALISM", "GEOPOLITICAL_LINKAGE", "TEMPORAL_LINKAGE"], "newValue": ["STRUCTURAL_ANALYSIS", "RELIGIOUS_INTERPRETATION", "DIPLOMATIC_HISTORY"]}], "_unsyncedEdits": true}

